# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [0.1.1] - 2026-05-02

### Breaking Changes

- Rename environment variables to per-adapter nested namespaces — update existing `.env` files to the new naming convention before upgrading
- Replace bookmark-centric job submission and response fields with `source_ref` and manifest v2.0 payload format
- Rename `bookmarks` database table to `sources` — run `alembic upgrade head` before starting the service

### Added

- Add `Orchestrator` with injected fetch and convert dispatch, making adapter implementations swappable without modifying worker logic
- Add core ports package (protocols, types, registries, `SourceRef`) and discrete fetcher and converter adapter packages
- Add wiring package that assembles role-specific runtime configurations at startup
- Add `source_ref` (canonical identifier) and `source_ref_hash` (deduplication key) columns to the sources schema, both `NOT NULL`
- Add `converter_name` and `config_snapshot` fields to `ProcessResult` for result-to-configuration traceability
- Add hermetic test defaults: `env_file=None` and `app.state.config` injection before lifespan runs so local `.env` files do not affect test outcomes
- Add experimental Claimify pipeline for extracting atomic claims from source text (not yet wired into the main ingestion flow)

### Changed

- Base deduplication on canonical `SourceRef` values, improving idempotency across retries and re-submissions
- Expand pip-audit test coverage

### Fixed

- Fix fetch pipeline edge cases in HTTP error handling and `dotenv` loading
- Fix S3 artifact key storage — `markdown_key` and `manifest_key` now hold bare keys without path prefixes
- Fix suggestions job guard to use `BoundedSemaphore`, preventing over-subscription under concurrent load
- Fix import layering, HTML injection, and Source validation in the warnings subsystem

---

## [0.1.0] - 2026-04-14

### Added

- Add document conversion pipeline: fetch sources from KaraKeep, convert with Docling, store Markdown output and manifests in S3
- Add support for arXiv papers, URLs, and pre-crawled archive assets as conversion inputs
- Add GPU-aware subprocess scheduling for concurrent conversion jobs without GPU memory contention
- Add config snapshot recording per job — re-submitting the same source with the same configuration returns the cached result rather than reconverting
- Add REST API for job submission, status polling (atomic, no N+1 queries), retry, cancel, and aggregated status counts
- Add queue back-pressure to reject submissions when the worker is saturated
- Add HTMX jobs panel with sortable columns, bulk retry/cancel/delete, and date formatting
- Add stale job recovery at startup for jobs left in `running` state across restarts
- Add graceful shutdown on `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT` that drains in-flight jobs before exiting
- Add startup validation that checks external service availability before the worker begins polling
- Add explicit `retryable` attribute to all exception classes — non-retryable failures are not requeued
- Add subprocess traceback capture; failure detail is stored in the database for operator review
- Add Alembic migrations from a baseline schema with round-trip correctness tests
- Add Litestream continuous SQLite replication to S3 for point-in-time recovery
- Add liveness (`/health/live`) and readiness (`/health/ready`) health check endpoints
- Add MLflow tracing for upstream LLM and embedding calls with span-level detail
- Add non-root, multi-stage container image
- Add Podman Compose configuration for local and self-hosted deployment
- Add whitespace normalization for consistent Markdown output at document boundaries
- Add Granite 4.0-3B Vision model support with classification-based prompt routing
- Add ArXiv client with async support, automatic batching for metadata requests, enhanced ID validation, and context manager semantics
- Add review-first cleanup workflow for stale KaraKeep and AIZK entries

### Fixed

- Fix SQLite write safety with connection serialization
- Fix N+1 job listing query with eager loading
- Fix S3 hash deduplication and cancellation ordering edge cases in the worker

### Security

- Update dependencies to resolve known vulnerabilities detected by pip-audit

